              "type": "text",
              "text": "<p><strong><strong>The Art Worlds of Spain and the United Kingdom</strong></strong> brings together two leading voices from the international art scene: Philip Hook, Senior Director at Sotheby's and celebrated author on the art market, and Alia Al-Senussi, renowned curator, cultural strategist and advisor to major global arts institutions. Together, they will explore the artistic, institutional and commercial connections between Spain and the United Kingdom, examining how ideas, collectors, museums and cultural networks shape the contemporary art landscape.</p><p>Drawing on their extensive experience across museums, auction houses, biennials and cultural organisations, Hook and Al-Senussi will discuss the evolving role of art in society, the global circulation of cultural influence, and the opportunities and challenges facing artists and institutions today. This lively conversation offers a unique opportunity to gain insider perspectives on two interconnected art worlds and their place within an increasingly international cultural ecosystem.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Philip Hook</strong></strong> is one of the art world's most respected specialists, writers and commentators. A Board Member and Senior Director of Impressionist &amp; Modern Art at Sotheby's in London, he has spent more than four decades at the heart of the international art market, advising collectors and handling some of the world's most significant works of art. Before joining Sotheby's, he worked at Christie's in the 19th Century Paintings Department, helping to establish his reputation as an expert in European art and the history of collecting.</p><p>Alongside his distinguished career as an auctioneer and art specialist, Hook is a celebrated author whose books explore the relationships between art, taste, money and power. His acclaimed non-fiction works include <em><em>Breakfast at Sotheby's: An A-Z of the Art World</em></em> (2013), named a Book of the Year by <em><em>The Sunday Times</em></em>, <em><em>The Spectator</em></em>, the <em><em>Financial Times</em></em>, <em><em>The Guardian</em></em> and the <em><em>Mail on Sunday</em></em>. He has since published several bestselling titles, including <em><em>The Ultimate Trophy: How the Impressionist Painting Conquered the World</em></em> and <em><em>Rogues' Gallery: A History of Art and Its Dealers</em></em>, both praised for their wit, insight and deep knowledge of the art market.</p><p>Hook is also the author of five novels and has been a familiar face on British television, appearing regularly on the BBC's <em><em>Antiques Roadshow</em></em>. Renowned for making the art world accessible to wider audiences, he combines scholarly expertise with a gift for storytelling, offering unique perspectives on artists, collectors, dealers and the cultural forces that shape the value of art. Today, he continues to play a leading role in the international art market while writing and speaking on art history, collecting and the evolution of taste.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Alia Al-Senussi</strong></strong><em><em>, PhD, is a leading figure in the contemporary art world, with a particular emphasis in her academic, personal, and professional work on visual arts and culture in the Middle East. She holds a doctorate in Politics from SOAS, University of London, where her research analysed the nexus of soft power and cultural diplomacy within networks of patronage.</em></em></p><p><em><em>Dr Al-Senussi is a founding member of the Tate’s Acquisitions Committee for the Middle East and North Africa, the Board of 1:54 The African Art Fair, and the Middle East Circle of the Guggenheim. Among her many leadership roles, she is the Founding Co-Chair of the LACMA Global Ambassadors and the Founding Chairperson of the K11 International Council (2023–2026). She is also a member of the Tate Modern Advisory Council, the Board of the ICA London, the Serpentine Future Contemporaries, and the Strategic Advisory Council of the Delfina Foundation. Most recently, she joined the Bukhara Biennial Advisory Board.</em></em></p><p><em><em>Dr Al-Senussi serves as Senior Advisor, International Outreach, and VIP Representative for the United Kingdom, as well as the Middle East and North Africa, for Art Basel. She also serves as a Senior Advisor to the Saudi Ministry of Culture, focusing on work with the Diriyah Biennale Foundation. Her most recent appointment is as Senior Advisor to the Uzbekistan Art and Culture Development Foundation (ACDF).</em></em></p><p><em><em>Dr Al-Senussi is a Visiting Professor at VCU Qatar and a regular lecturer at Sotheby’s Institute of Art and universities worldwide, including St Andrews, Brown, and IE Madrid. She is also a frequent panellist and moderator at international conferences and collaborates with organisations such as the Milken Institute.</em></em></p><p><em><em>In 2026, Dr Al-Senussi received a number of awards, including the Aiglon College Values in Action Award (AVIA) winner, AWITA Honours Leaders in Culture, and the K11 Art Foundation Prize: Honouring Global Visionaries, awarded in recognition of her role as Founding Chairperson Emerita.</em></em></p><p><br></p><p>Event organised in collaboration with IE University.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Los mundos del arte en España y el Reino Unido</strong></strong> reúne a dos destacadas figuras del panorama artístico internacional: Philip Hook, Senior Director de Sotheby's y reconocido autor sobre el mercado del arte, y Alia Al-Senussi, comisaria, asesora cultural y una de las voces más influyentes del sector a nivel global. Juntos explorarán los vínculos históricos y contemporáneos entre España y el Reino Unido, analizando cómo artistas, coleccionistas, museos e instituciones han contribuido a modelar ambos ecosistemas culturales.</p><p>A partir de sus amplias trayectorias en museos, casas de subastas, bienales y organizaciones culturales, Hook y Al-Senussi reflexionarán sobre el papel del arte en la sociedad actual, la circulación internacional de las ideas y las nuevas oportunidades y desafíos que afrontan las instituciones culturales. Una conversación única para comprender mejor dos mundos del arte profundamente conectados en un contexto cada vez más global.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Philip Hook</strong></strong> es uno de los especialistas en arte y escritores más reconocidos del Reino Unido. Actualmente es miembro del Consejo de Administración y Senior Director del departamento de Arte Impresionista y Moderno de Sotheby's en Londres, donde ha desarrollado gran parte de su carrera asesorando a coleccionistas y participando en la venta de algunas de las obras más importantes del mercado internacional. Anteriormente trabajó en Christie's, en el departamento de Pintura del Siglo XIX.</p><p>Además de su labor en el mundo del arte, Hook es un prolífico autor y divulgador. Ha escrito cinco novelas y numerosos libros sobre el mercado del arte, el coleccionismo y la historia de las obras maestras. Su libro <em><em>Breakfast at Sotheby's: An A-Z of the Art World</em></em> (2013) fue seleccionado como Libro del Año por <em><em>The Sunday Times</em></em>, <em><em>The Spectator</em></em>, <em><em>Financial Times</em></em>, <em><em>The Guardian</em></em> y <em><em>Mail on Sunday</em></em>. Entre sus publicaciones más conocidas figuran también <em><em>The Ultimate Trophy: How the Impressionist Painting Conquered the World</em></em> y <em><em>Rogues' Gallery: A History of Art and Its Dealers</em></em>.</p><p>Conocido por su agudeza, humor y capacidad para acercar el arte a públicos amplios, Hook ha aparecido regularmente en el programa de la BBC <em><em>Antiques Roadshow</em></em> y es un conferenciante habitual sobre historia del arte, coleccionismo y mercado artístico. Su doble trayectoria como experto y escritor le ha convertido en una de las voces más influyentes para entender cómo el gusto, el dinero y la cultura han configurado el mundo del arte moderno.</p><p><strong><strong>Alia Al-Senussi, PhD</strong></strong>, es una destacada figura del arte contemporáneo internacional, con especial atención, tanto en su trabajo académico como profesional, a las artes visuales y la cultura de Oriente Medio. Se doctoró en Política por la SOAS University of London, donde su investigación analizó la relación entre el poder blando, la diplomacia cultural y las redes de mecenazgo.</p><p>La Dra. Al-Senussi es miembro fundadora del Comité de Adquisiciones para Oriente Medio y Norte de África de la Tate, del consejo de la feria de arte africano <strong><strong>1:54</strong></strong>, y del <strong><strong>Middle East Circle</strong></strong> del Museo Guggenheim. Entre sus numerosos cargos de liderazgo, destaca como cofundadora y copresidenta de los <strong><strong>LACMA Global Ambassadors</strong></strong> y como presidenta fundadora del <strong><strong>K11 International Council</strong></strong> (2023-2026). También forma parte del Consejo Asesor de Tate Modern, del consejo directivo del ICA de Londres, de <strong><strong>Serpentine Future Contemporaries</strong></strong> y del Consejo Asesor Estratégico de la <strong><strong>Delfina Foundation</strong></strong>. Más recientemente, se incorporó al consejo asesor de la <strong><strong>Bienal de Bujará</strong></strong>.</p><p>Asimismo, ejerce como asesora principal de Proyección Internacional y representante VIP para el Reino Unido, Oriente Medio y el Norte de África de <strong><strong>Art Basel</strong></strong>. También es asesora principal del Ministerio de Cultura de Arabia Saudí, con especial dedicación a la <strong><strong>Diriyah Biennale Foundation</strong></strong>, y recientemente ha sido nombrada asesora principal de la <strong><strong>Fundación para el Desarrollo del Arte y la Cultura de Uzbekistán (ACDF)</strong></strong>.</p><p>La Dra. Al-Senussi es profesora visitante en <strong><strong>VCU Qatar</strong></strong> y conferenciante habitual en el <strong><strong>Sotheby’s Institute of Art</strong></strong> y en universidades de todo el mundo, entre ellas St Andrews, Brown e IE Madrid. Participa regularmente como ponente y moderadora en conferencias internacionales y colabora con organizaciones como el <strong><strong>Milken Institute</strong></strong>.</p><p>En 2026 recibió diversos reconocimientos, entre ellos el <strong><strong>Aiglon College Values in Action Award (AVIA)</strong></strong>, el premio <strong><strong>AWITA Honours Leaders in Culture</strong></strong> y el <strong><strong>K11 Art Foundation Prize: Honouring Global Visionaries</strong></strong>, concedido en reconocimiento a su labor como presidenta fundadora emérita de dicha institución.</p><p><br></p><p>Evento organizado en colaboración con la Universidad ie.</p>",
